  "body_markdown": "Skip to content\n\nDental Implants\n\nDental Implant Surgery\n\nAll-on-4 Dental Implants\n\nFixed Teeth vs. Removable\n\nCost & Compare\n\nDental Implant FAQ\n\nAesthetics\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nPorcelain Veneers\n\nDental Crowns & Bridges\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nTreatments\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nOral Surgery\n\nEmergency Dentistry\n\nConditions We Treat\n\nWhat To Expect\n\nPatient Center\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nSmile Gallery\n\nWho We Are\n\nWhy Choose Us\n\nMeet Dr. Esam Nahlah\n\nMeet The Team\n\nVideo Library\n\nPatient Stories\n\nFor Doctors\n\nReferral Form\n\nContact Us\n\nBlog\n\nCurrent Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria: (703) 940-5410\n\nNew Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (571) 619-9442\n\nAlexandria: (571) 410-3430\n\nBook now\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## Can I Upgrade My Smile From Traditional Dentures To Implant Supported Dentures?\n\n\nNovember 14, 2023\n\n\n#### Share This Post\n\n\nTraditional dentures are made to replace missing teeth by sitting on the patients gums and being held in place by adhesives. While traditional dentures do give patients new teeth, they often become unstable and uncomfortable as the patients jawbone and facial structure begin to change because the missing tooth roots are no longer stimulating the jawbone.\n\nWhen people no longer want to wear traditional dentures, they can upgrade their smile to implant supported dentures in McLean, VA. Continue reading to learn more about why people will want to upgrade their smile to implant supported dentures.\n\n\n## How Will My Smile Be Upgraded From Traditional Dentures To Implant Supported Dentures In McLean, VA?\n\n\nWhen people are tired of wearing traditional dentures, then they can go to a skilled and trusted dental office to upgrade their smile to implant supported dentures. When beginning the implant supported denture procedure process, the patient’s mouth will first be evaluated to make sure it has enough jawbone density and volume to support their new smile.\n\nFor those who do not have enough jawbone density to support their implant supported dentures, they can first get treated with a bone grafting procedure. A bone grafting procedure restores the patients jawbone density and volume so that it can reliably support their implant supported dentures.\n\nNext, two or more dental implant posts can be strategically angled and placed in the patient’s jawbone. The dental implant posts are made to act like natural tooth roots, so when they are placed in the jawbone, they not only fuse (osseointegrate) with it, they become a permanent and stable part of their smile as well.\n\nAfter the dental implants have been securely placed in the patient’s jawbone, the denture can be securely attached to the dental implants. With the denture securely attached to the dental implants, patients will have a more stable and reliable new smile that allows them to eat, chew, speak, and smile comfortably.\n\n\n## See Us Now So We Can Upgrade Your Smile To Implant Supported Dentures In McLean, VA\n\n\nIf you don’t want to live with uncomfortable traditional dentures that no longer properly fit your mouth anymore, then you should come to our office to upgrade your smile to implant supported dentures. With implant supported dentures, dental implants are used to give you a secure new smile that will let you live your life normally.\n\nWhy wait to improve your smile with us? Get in contact with our doctors, Dr. Esam Nahlah and our exceptional team at our office to schedule an appointment today!\n\nPrevPreviousConsidering Getting Treated With All-On-4® Dental Implants In McLean, VA? This Is Why You Should\n\nNextHow Many Missing Teeth Can Dental Implants Replace?Next\n\n\n#### More To Explore\n\n\n\n### Unlock the Benefits of Dental Implants: Your Best Teeth Replacement Option\n\n\nTooth loss can become an unfortunate reality for many as we age. Thankfully, advancements in dental technology, like dental implants,\n\nRead More »\n\nOctober 26, 2024\n\n\n### Your Comprehensive Guide on Dental Implants: The Best Replacement of Tooth Solution\n\n\nDental implants in McLean, VA are small, and titanium posts are surgically placed in your jawbone underneath your gum line.\n\nOctober 20, 2024\n\n\n## You Are Welcome Here.\n\n\nSchedule your consultation today.\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddresses:\n\nTysons Corner\n\n7901 Jones Branch Dr., Suite 220\n\nMcLean, VA 22102\n\nNew Patients: (571) 619-9442\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria\n\n2855 Duke St,\n\nAlexandria, VA 22314\n\nNew Patients: (571) 410-3430\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 940-5410\n\n\n#### Hours\n\n\nMonday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nTuesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nWednesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nThursday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nFriday: 8:00am – 2:00pm\n\nSaturday: Closed\n\nSunday: Closed\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\nAll-On-4® Implants\n\nCrowns & Bridges\n\n\n#### About Us\n\n\nMeet the Doctor\n\nAbout Us\n\nBefore & After Photos\n\n2025 Dr. Nahlah. All rights reserved",
